# Tencent Q1 financial report: Profit only increased by 9%? Unpacking the AI core business hides 17%

Tencent’s Q1 revenue was 196.5 billion, 2.5 billion lower than market expectations.

But if you only draw conclusions after seeing this number, you will miss the most important new information in this financial report-Tencent has separated out its AI investment for the first time. After excluding the loss of AI products, core business profits increased by 17% and the profit margin was 43%.

In other words, Tencent's core engine is not slowing down, but making room for the "new passenger" AI.

Ma Huateng used a metaphor at today’s shareholders’ meeting:

> "It turned out that a year ago we thought we were on the boat, but then we found that the boat was leaking. Now we feel like we are standing on it, but we can't sit down. We still hope the boat can be faster."

This sentence is very honest. Tencent's AI progress is probably in this state - it has not fallen, but it is not stable yet.

> **Reading Tip**: Tencent’s financial report has two sets of profit figures. This article mainly uses "Non-IFRS profit", which is the profit after excluding one-time factors such as equity incentives and investment fluctuations, which can better reflect the true profitability of the core business.

