## 3. What truth did the management say?

In addition to financial report numbers, management's speeches at shareholder meetings and performance briefings are much more candid than in press releases.

**Ma Huateng talks about AI competitive strategy:**

> "You can't just look at what others are doing and just step over and seize other people's territory. We have done so in the past but basically failed in the end."

This sentence is tantamount to acknowledging Tencent’s past lessons of blindly following the trend in some fields (short video, e-commerce, etc.). In the context of AI, it means that Tencent will not engage in an arms race with general large models, but will focus on AI applications in scenarios where it has advantages (social networking, advertising, games).

**Liu Chiping’s self-criticism of Hunyuan:**

According to 36Kr, Liu Chiping internally commented that Hunyuan was "more like a test-taking exam, with good performance in individual subjects, but his secrets were revealed as soon as he entered the examination room, and many key abilities were lacking**".

Although Hunyuan 3 Preview topped the Token usage rankings on OpenRouter, this achievement was somewhat limited - limited promotion during the period, coupled with quota calls for internal business. The real test will be whether the product can retain external developers after the limited exemption period ends.

**Yuanbao’s real user data:**

Yuanbao’s MAU in March was approximately 57.35 million, but this number needs to be understood in context: the peak value exceeded 114 million during the Spring Festival (Tencent spent 1 billion on promotion), and fell quickly after the holiday. Net user additions in the first quarter were only about 8.2 million. For comparison, the average daily calls of Byte Doubao during the same period was about 30 times that of Hunyuan, with a net increase of about 100 million users in the first quarter.

The gap exists objectively. However, the management's attitude is to accept "slowness" and not rush to catch up: Ma Huateng said "play slowly and steadily", and Liu Chiping said "monetization will naturally occur as usage increases."

**Liu Chiping responded to rumors of layoffs:**

> "There is definitely no big layoff plan. Tencent is not the same as Silicon Valley companies."

